## Setup

Let $L = \{0, 1, \ldots, 99\}^2$ with center $c = (49.5, 49.5)$. For each lattice point $v$, write $v = c + (a_v, b_v)$ where $a_v, b_v \in \{-49.5, -48.5, \ldots, 49.5\}$ are half-integers.

## Upper Bound

**Key Inequality.** For any simple polygon $P$ with vertices $v_1, \ldots, v_k$ and any point $c$:
$$\operatorname{Area}(P) \leq \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{k} |v_i - c|^2.$$

*Proof.* Set $u_i = v_i - c$. By the shoelace formula and translation invariance:
$$\operatorname{Area}(P) = \frac{1}{2}\left|\sum_{i} u_i \times u_{i+1}\right| \leq \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i} |u_i \times u_{i+1}| = \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i} |u_i||u_{i+1}||\sin\theta_i| \leq \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i} |u_i||u_{i+1}| \leq \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i} \frac{|u_i|^2 + |u_{i+1}|^2}{2} = \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i} |u_i|^2.$$
The last equality uses the cyclic sum identity $\sum_i(|u_i|^2 + |u_{i+1}|^2) = 2\sum_i |u_i|^2$. $\square$

**Equality** holds iff $P$ is a square centered at $c$: (i) all cross products same sign (convex), (ii) $|\sin\theta_i|=1$ for all $i$ (all angles $90°$, forcing $k=4$), (iii) $|u_i|=|u_{i+1}|$ for all $i$ (equidistant from $c$).

